234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (When I came to Yale for my MPH, I was deeply inspired by the rich tapestry of people that made up the Greater New Haven community. I knew I wanted to serve in some way, but I wasn't quite sure what that would look like. Early on, Dr. Lagarde introduced me to the world of community health organizations and, in her characteristic way, made me feel like the world was my oyster. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (Every week, I have been inspired by people who quietly go far beyond the call of duty. The volunteers answering phones after class. The interpreters and clinical students who stay late so a patient feels heard. The attendings who linger long after clinic ends to answer just one more question. The ancillary departments that recognize a diagnosis is only one part of a patient's story, helping address the social factors that shape health. Whether you stand on the front lines of patient care or work tirelessly behind the scenes, every single one of you has shaped someone's healthcare journey.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (If you know me, you know that HAVEN has become my version of Disney. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (There is something magical about Saturday mornings here. Hundreds of volunteers choose each weekend to show up for neighbors they have never met. Somewhere between the controlled chaos, the laughter in the hallways, and the unwavering commitment to our patients, HAVEN became, well, a haven.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (As I begin a new chapter right down the road, I leave with one small request: never lose sight of the trust our patients place in us. They invite us into some of the most vulnerable moments of their lives, and that trust should never become routine. Our work is far from easy. Sometimes it is frustrating, confusing, or painfully slow. But it matters. At HAVEN, you have the opportunity to change the trajectory of someone's life, not always through a grand gesture, but through a returned phone call, a completed form, a reassuring conversation, or simply refusing to give up on someone when the system has.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
240 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (Thank you for believing in our mission, for believing in one another and in our patients, and for reminding me every clinic day what compassionate and interdisciplinary healthcare can look like. I can't wait to see how the world becomes your oyster and know that I will always be cheering you on from the sidelines!)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
